# Export/import workflow

`pebbles export` serializes the issue set as a JSON bundle, a flat CSV, or a
Markdown document; `pebbles import` loads a JSON bundle additively.

Fixture store: an epic (444, User Authentication Epic) with two children
(111 Login button, 333 JWT auth) and two orphans (555 Export users to CSV,
done; 222 User can login). A second, empty store lives at `blank/.pebbles`
for the round-trip into a fresh store. `partial.json` carries two new
issues, one of which references a target that exists only in the store
(kept) and one that exists nowhere (dropped with a warning).

## Export JSON to a file

`export --output` writes the bundle and prints a confirmation; the file is
asserted byte-for-byte in `.out/export.json`.

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles export json -o export.json
✓ Exported 5 issue(s) to export.json

```

## Export CSV to stdout

r[verify csv-schema]
```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles export csv
id,title,description,status,issue_type,tags,relationships,metadata
"11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111","Login button doesn't respond on mobile","The login button doesn't respond to clicks on mobile devices","todo","bug","[]","[{""relation_type"":""part_of"",""target_id"":""44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444""}]","{}"
"22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222","User can login with email and password","","todo","usecase","[]","[]","{}"
"33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333","JWT token authentication system","Design and implement JWT-based authentication","todo","design","[]","[{""relation_type"":""part_of"",""target_id"":""44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444""}]","{}"
"44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444","User Authentication Epic","Implement complete user authentication system","todo","epic","[]","[]","{}"
"55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555","Export users to CSV","","done","usecase","[]","[]","{}"

```

## Export Markdown to stdout

r[verify export-markdown] Children render under their epic, done issues get
`[x]`, and non-epic issues without a part_of relationship land in Orphans
(both sorted by title).

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles export markdown
# Pebbles Export

## Epic: User Authentication Epic

- [ ] 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333 [des] [todo] JWT token authentication system
- [ ] 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 [bug] [todo] Login button doesn't respond on mobile

## Orphans

- [x] 55555555-5555-5555-5555-555555555555 [uc] [done] Export users to CSV
- [ ] 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222 [uc] [todo] User can login with email and password

```

## Round-trip: the bundle imports into a fresh store

r[verify import-semantics]
```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=blank/.pebbles pebbles import export.json
✓ Imported 5 issue(s) from export.json

```

## Import is additive, preserving relationships to store issues

r[verify import-semantics] The new issue keeps its part_of link to the epic
that already exists in the store; the relationship to a target that exists
neither in the bundle nor in the store is dropped with a warning.

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles import partial.json
Warning: Import dropped relationship required_for -> 99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999 from 'API key rotation': target not found in the bundle or the store
✓ Imported 2 issue(s) from partial.json

```

## A bundle colliding with the store is rejected atomically

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles import export.json
? 1
Error: Issue 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 already exists in this store; import is additive and never overwrites existing issues

```

## Duplicate ids inside a bundle are rejected

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=blank/.pebbles pebbles import duplicate.json
? 1
Error: Export bundle contains duplicate issue id: 88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888

```

## A JSON file that is not an export bundle is rejected

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles import .pebbles/index.json
? 1
Error: Not a pebbles export bundle: missing "format" field

```
